From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [CPU] Add guest hooks: host code before a guest instruction

Title code can register a host callback for a guest address before the
title's code is translated. The PPC HIR builder emits a CALL_EXTERN to a
per-hook builtin right before that instruction; CALL_EXTERN is volatile, so
every guest register is in the PPCContext during the callback and changes
are picked up by the instruction that follows. Hooks only run while the
table is active, so code translated for a previous title stays inert.
